Hello All,

A few weeks back, as part of a project to make a PAN client on a nokia
phone, we started porting BlueZ to Symbian (nokia, sony ericson etc)

You can read about it here:

https://blogs.forum.nokia.com/view_entry.html?id=719

Also, you can check out the sources etc, here:

bluspan.sourceforge.net

This is the first compile, still of course, issues regarding porting
the PAND and BNEP to Symbian (like no "ARGC and ARGV")

This project is supported by Nokia, as an official project and
experiment and blogged on their site as one of only 10 or so blogs.

It's our hope BlueZ will become the basis for the client we want to
build and we'd love to share our development with the BlueZ community.
Since Cell phones out number UNIX machines like 100 to 1 maybe some
day, we'll say "And Some Users of BlueZ Run LINUX "

So, heads up, Kostya is writing a post about the first time he got a
compile under Symbian, will write about some issues he's facing, and
post that in the next day or to, I'll ask him to update the CVS
tonight if any of you want to download it and check it out.

And finally, I'd like to take this opportunity to thank the developers
of BlueZ for the work they've done. Certainly, with this project, we
climb on the shoulders of Giants to reach something new. Thanks People
with your help, people will be using their computer to connect their
cell phones to the internet and not the other way around.

If you can help a little more by mentoring Kostya, sharing your
insight and knowledge by joining the effort, commenting in the blog,
or anything else, thanks in advance.

David

